# Forgejo 15.0.7 (image codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo:15.0.7) environment
# schema (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# The compose used to pin the floating major tag `:11`. On 2026-09-04
# (research date) that tag still resolved (index digest
# sha256:946243edbab116d5bb78b73ea68af6f3d69229ba1b1ed958dd82c3481167f3e0,
# amd64 config created 2026-07-09, org.opencontainers.image.version=11.0.16)
# but the 11.x line is now listed as DISCONTINUED on
# https://forgejo.org/releases/, so no more patches, including security ones.
# Forgejo runs two lines at a time: `latest` (v16.0.3, supported to
# 2026-10-29) and LTS (v15.0.7, supported to 2027-07-15). Self-hosting wants
# the LTS, so the pin moved to the newest LTS patch, 15.0.7, which is also
# the security-current one: 15.0.7 and 16.0.3 were released the same day
# (2026-08-20) as a coordinated security release (repo-specific /
# public-only token access to `pulls/{index}/update`, `pull_request_target`
# reusable-workflow expansion, owner-as-collaboration-access-mode). Index
# digest sha256:1f9c1a9880425614267832ce437f8ae5f5b69e1f3219f38fc468fc37e48c1919,
# linux/amd64 + arm64 + arm. The registry still ships newer tags for both
# lines, so the repo is alive.
#
# Source: the v15.0.7 source tree, all three configuration mechanisms, not a
# blanket os.Getenv grep (which finds almost nothing, because Forgejo's real
# config surface is app.ini, not the environment):
#
#  1. `FORGEJO__<section>__<KEY>` -> app.ini. docker/root/etc/s6/gitea/setup
#     runs `environment-to-ini --config ${GITEA_CUSTOM}/conf/app.ini` on
#     EVERY container start, so these values always win over what is already
#     in app.ini. The decoder is setting.EnvironmentToConfig
#     (modules/setting/config_env.go): the accepted prefix is the regexp
#     `^(FORGEJO|GITEA)__`, so GITEA__ still works identically. FORGEJO__ is
#     the name this fork documents and the one used below. Strip the prefix,
#     split section from key on the first `__`, lowercase the section. A `.`
#     in a section or key is written `_0x2E_`
#     (`FORGEJO__log_0x2E_console__COLORIZE` sets `[log.console] COLORIZE`).
#     A `__FILE` suffix means "read the value from the file at this path"
#     (one trailing newline stripped), the docker-secrets form, available
#     for EVERY key, e.g. FORGEJO__database__PASSWD__FILE=/run/secrets/db.
#     Caveat: an empty value is still applied, writing an EMPTY app.ini key,
#     which is not the same as leaving the key out. Only set a FORGEJO__
#     variable you actually want written.
#
#  2. Plain variables read by the image's shell, not by Forgejo:
#     docker/root/usr/bin/entrypoint (USER, USER_UID, USER_GID),
#     docker/root/etc/s6/gitea/setup (the envsubst pass over
#     /etc/templates/app.ini) and docker/root/etc/s6/openssh/setup (the
#     envsubst pass over /etc/templates/sshd_config). The app.ini template
#     pass is FIRST-BOOT ONLY: it runs solely when
#     /data/gitea/conf/app.ini does not exist yet, so on an existing data
#     volume those variables do nothing. The sshd_config pass runs on every
#     boot.
#
#  3. The short list of variables the Go binary itself reads:
#     GITEA_WORK_DIR / FORGEJO_WORK_DIR and GITEA_CUSTOM / FORGEJO_CUSTOM
#     (modules/setting/path.go, GITEA_* checked first, FORGEJO_* as the
#     fallback), GITEA_RUN_MODE and GITEA_I_AM_BEING_UNSAFE_RUNNING_AS_ROOT
#     (modules/setting/setting.go:169-171; these two have NO FORGEJO_ alias).
#
# Defaults below are the ones in modules/setting/*.go at v15.0.7. Forgejo is
# a Gitea fork that has diverged; everything here was re-read against
# Forgejo's own source, and these are the places where copying Gitea's
# answer would have been wrong:
#
#   * `[server] OFFLINE_MODE` still exists in Forgejo and defaults to TRUE
#     (server.go:294). Gitea deleted the setting. It is the reason a fresh
#     Forgejo never calls out to Gravatar or a CDN.
#   * `[security] COOKIE_REMEMBER_NAME` defaults to `persistent`
#     (security.go:117). It was renamed in v15.0.0 to be brand independent;
#     every user has to log in again after that upgrade unless the old
#     `gitea_incredible` is set back explicitly.
#   * `[service] REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW` is a plain bool here (service.go:212).
#     Gitea's `expensive` mode does not exist.
#   * `[database]` supports mysql, postgres and sqlite3 only
#     (database.go:21-23), not mssql.
#   * `[database] MAX_OPEN_CONNS` defaults to 30, not 0/unlimited
#     (database.go:99).
#   * `[actions] DEFAULT_ACTIONS_URL` defaults to Forgejo's own action
#     mirror, data.forgejo.org (actions.go:35,60), and takes a full URL as
#     well as the keywords `github` and `self`.
#   * There is NO runner registration token variable. Gitea's
#     GITEA_RUNNER_REGISTRATION_TOKEN[_FILE] has no counterpart anywhere in
#     the Forgejo tree; runners are registered with a token taken from the
#     admin UI or `forgejo forgejo-cli actions register`.
#   * `[security] GLOBAL_TWO_FACTOR_REQUIREMENT` and `[federation]` are
#     Forgejo-only additions.
#   * GITEA_APP_INI / GITEA_TEMP exist ONLY in the rootless image
#     (Dockerfile.rootless). This template runs the ROOT image, whose s6
#     scripts hardcode ${GITEA_CUSTOM}/conf/app.ini, so setting them here
#     does nothing. Declared anyway, empty, so the difference is visible.
#
# app.ini has several hundred settings across ~60 sections; enumerating them
# all here would be noise. This file covers what the compose sets plus the
# sections an operator actually touches on a self-hosted instance (server,
# database, security, service, mailer, actions, federation, log). The
# complete surface is upstream-documented in the Configuration Cheat Sheet
# linked below. Any key on that page can be set here as
# FORGEJO__<section>__<KEY>.
#
# The compose prompts for FORGEJO_URL and POSTGRES_PASSWORD, which is all a
# fresh install needs. Nothing sets INSTALL_LOCK or SECRET_KEY, so the first
# visit to the site shows Forgejo's install page, where the admin account is
# created; the database fields there arrive pre-filled from the compose.

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("Forgejo Configuration Cheat Sheet", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/config-cheat-sheet/)
# ---

# ─── Platform prompt keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The two values otterdeploy asks for before the stack is created. Each is
# threaded by the compose into the container variables that carry it.

# Full public URL of this Forgejo, scheme included and trailing slash kept
# (`https` + `://` + the host you serve it on + `/`). Clone URLs, webhook
# payloads, avatar links, OAuth redirects and Actions callbacks are all
# built from it, so a wrong value produces a site that renders but hands out
# unusable URLs. The compose passes it as FORGEJO__server__ROOT_URL below.
# @required
# @type=url
# @docs("Installation with Docker", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/installation/docker/)
FORGEJO_URL=

# Password for the bundled PostgreSQL's `forgejo` role. The compose puts the
# same value in the database container's POSTGRES_PASSWORD and in
# FORGEJO__database__PASSWD; the two must stay identical or Forgejo cannot
# connect. Generate with `openssl rand -base64 24`.
# @required
# @sensitive
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ─── Bundled PostgreSQL (service `db`) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Read by the postgres:17-alpine image's own entrypoint, only on the very
# first boot with an empty data directory. Changing them later does not
# rename anything. POSTGRES_PASSWORD is the prompt key declared above.

# Role the entrypoint creates and that Forgejo logs in as. Mirrored by
# FORGEJO__database__USER.
# @docs("postgres image environment variables", https://hub.docker.com/_/postgres)
POSTGRES_USER=forgejo

# Database the entrypoint creates. Mirrored by FORGEJO__database__NAME.
POSTGRES_DB=forgejo

# ─── Database ([database]) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which database driver to use. The compose runs PostgreSQL, so `postgres`.
# Leaving this at the image default (`sqlite3`, from the first-boot
# template) would silently ignore the bundled database. `mssql` is a Gitea
# type that Forgejo does not have.
# @required
# @type=enum(postgres, mysql, sqlite3)
# @docs("Database preparation", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/installation/database-preparation/)
FORGEJO__database__DB_TYPE=postgres

# Database endpoint as `host:port` (or an absolute path for a unix socket).
# Set by the compose to the bundled Postgres service. Platform-owned.
# @required
FORGEJO__database__HOST=${{stack.db.HOST}}:5432

# Database name. Must match the bundled Postgres's POSTGRES_DB.
# @required
FORGEJO__database__NAME=forgejo

# Database role. Must match the bundled Postgres's POSTGRES_USER.
# @required
FORGEJO__database__USER=forgejo

# Database password. Set by the compose from POSTGRES_PASSWORD; keep the two
# in sync. For a docker secret use FORGEJO__database__PASSWD__FILE, or point
# FORGEJO__database__PASSWD_URI at a `file:` URI instead.
# @required
# @sensitive
FORGEJO__database__PASSWD=${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}

# Reads the password from a URI (`file:/run/secrets/forgejo_db`) rather than
# inline. Setting both this and PASSWD is a fatal error at startup.
FORGEJO__database__PASSWD_URI=

# libpq sslmode for the connection. Default `disable`, which is what the
# bundled Postgres speaks (plaintext on the private stack network). Only
# raise this for an external managed database.
# @type=enum(disable, require, verify-ca, verify-full)
FORGEJO__database__SSL_MODE=disable

# PostgreSQL schema to use inside NAME. Empty means the role's default
# search_path (normally `public`).
FORGEJO__database__SCHEMA=

# Log every SQL statement. Very noisy; for debugging a slow instance only.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__database__LOG_SQL=false

# Log a warning for any query slower than this. Duration string ("5s",
# "500ms").
FORGEJO__database__SLOW_QUERY_THRESHOLD=5s

# Connection pool sizing. Forgejo caps MAX_OPEN_CONNS at 30 by default (0
# means unlimited); raise MAX_IDLE_CONNS on a busy instance so connections
# are reused rather than reopened.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__database__MAX_OPEN_CONNS=30
# @type=number
FORGEJO__database__MAX_IDLE_CONNS=2

# Durations a pooled connection may live, or sit idle, before it is
# recycled. `0` means forever; a proxy or managed database that closes idle
# connections needs a finite value here.
FORGEJO__database__CONN_MAX_LIFETIME=0
FORGEJO__database__CONN_MAX_IDLETIME=0

# How many times, and how long apart, Forgejo retries the initial database
# connection at startup. The bundled Postgres is usually accepting
# connections well inside the default 10 x 3s window.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__database__DB_RETRIES=10
FORGEJO__database__DB_RETRY_BACKOFF=3s

# Rows Forgejo fetches per batch when iterating a large table (migrations,
# reindexing). Lower it if memory is tight.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__database__ITERATE_BUFFER_SIZE=50

# Run schema migrations automatically at startup. Turning this off means an
# upgrade refuses to start until you migrate by hand. Only for operators who
# deliberately gate migrations.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__database__AUTO_MIGRATION=true

# ─── Server & URLs ([server]) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# The public URL, set by the compose from the FORGEJO_URL prompt key.
# @required
# @type=url
# @docs("Reverse proxy setup", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/setup/reverse-proxy/)
FORGEJO__server__ROOT_URL=${FORGEJO_URL}

# How Forgejo itself serves: `http` (default) is correct behind
# otterdeploy's TLS-terminating proxy. `https` makes Forgejo terminate TLS
# itself, and then CERT_FILE/KEY_FILE (or ACME) are required.
# @type=enum(http, https, fcgi, http+unix, fcgi+unix)
FORGEJO__server__PROTOCOL=http

# Bare hostname (no scheme, no port) used for SSH clone URLs and as the base
# for the default NO_REPLY_ADDRESS. Usually the host part of ROOT_URL.
FORGEJO__server__DOMAIN=localhost

# Address the HTTP server binds to inside the container. `0.0.0.0` is what
# the container network needs; narrowing it makes the published port
# unreachable.
FORGEJO__server__HTTP_ADDR=0.0.0.0

# Port the HTTP server listens on. The compose exposes container port 3000
# with no override, so this is that port's twin. Change one without the other
# and routing breaks.
# @type=port
FORGEJO__server__HTTP_PORT=3000

# TLS certificate and key paths inside the container, used only when
# PROTOCOL=https. Mount them into the container first.
FORGEJO__server__CERT_FILE=
FORGEJO__server__KEY_FILE=

# Blocks every outbound request for third-party avatars, badges and other
# remote assets, so nothing leaks to Gravatar or a CDN. Forgejo defaults
# this to TRUE (Gitea removed the setting entirely); turn it off only if you
# actually want federated avatars.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__server__OFFLINE_MODE=true

# Prefix static assets are served from, for putting JS/CSS on a CDN. Empty
# means "serve them from ROOT_URL's sub-path", which is what you want unless
# you have a CDN.
FORGEJO__server__STATIC_URL_PREFIX=

# What anonymous visitors see at `/`. Any other value is treated as a
# literal path to redirect to.
# @type=enum(home, explore, organizations, login)
FORGEJO__server__LANDING_PAGE=home

# Turn off Git over SSH entirely. The root image runs an OpenSSH daemon on
# container port 22 (see the sshd variables at the end of this file); this
# compose does not publish that port, so SSH clones are unreachable until
# you expose it.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__server__DISABLE_SSH=false

# Use Forgejo's own built-in SSH server instead of the image's OpenSSH
# daemon. With the built-in server, SSH_LISTEN_PORT is a port inside the
# Forgejo process and no sshd is involved.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__server__START_SSH_SERVER=false

# Hostname shown in SSH clone URLs. Empty falls back to DOMAIN. Set it only
# when SSH arrives on a different name than HTTP.
FORGEJO__server__SSH_DOMAIN=

# Port shown in SSH clone URLs (what users connect to from outside), and the
# port sshd/the built-in server actually listens on inside the container.
# They differ whenever a proxy or a published-port remap sits in between.
# @type=port
FORGEJO__server__SSH_PORT=22
# @type=port
FORGEJO__server__SSH_LISTEN_PORT=22

# Username in SSH clone URLs (`git@host:org/repo.git`). BUILTIN_SSH_SERVER_USER
# empty falls back to the process's run user, which is `git` in this image,
# and SSH_USER in turn falls back to BUILTIN_SSH_SERVER_USER.
FORGEJO__server__BUILTIN_SSH_SERVER_USER=
FORGEJO__server__SSH_USER=

# Serve Git LFS from this instance. Off by default; large-file workflows
# need it on, and objects then land under the data volume at /data/git/lfs.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("Storage configuration", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/setup/storage/)
FORGEJO__server__LFS_START_SERVER=false

# ─── Security ([security]) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `true` skips the web installer. This compose leaves it unset, so the first
# visit shows the install page and creates the admin account there. Set it
# to true only together with SECRET_KEY and a database that is already
# populated, otherwise you lock yourself out of an uninitialised instance.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("Authentication setup", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/setup/authentication/)
FORGEJO__security__INSTALL_LOCK=

# Key used to encrypt secrets at rest (2FA secrets, mirror and OAuth
# credentials, Actions secrets, package registry tokens). Generated by the
# installer on first run and written into app.ini; supply your own only if
# you are restoring an existing instance, and never change it afterwards, or
# the old ciphertext becomes unreadable. Prefer SECRET_KEY_URI for a
# file-backed secret.
# @sensitive
FORGEJO__security__SECRET_KEY=

# Read SECRET_KEY from a URI instead of inline, e.g.
# `file:/run/secrets/forgejo_secret_key`. Setting both this and SECRET_KEY
# is a fatal error at startup.
FORGEJO__security__SECRET_KEY_URI=

# JWT signing key for Forgejo's internal API (the one git hooks call back
# on). Generated on first run; regenerating it invalidates in-flight hook
# calls. INTERNAL_TOKEN_URI is the file-backed form, and setting both is
# fatal.
# @sensitive
FORGEJO__security__INTERNAL_TOKEN=
FORGEJO__security__INTERNAL_TOKEN_URI=

# Require two-factor authentication instance-wide. `admin` forces it for
# site administrators only, `all` for everybody; anything unrecognised is
# read as `none`. Forgejo-only setting.
# @type=enum(none, admin, all)
FORGEJO__security__GLOBAL_TWO_FACTOR_REQUIREMENT=none

# Name of the "remember me" cookie. Renamed to the brand-independent
# `persistent` in v15.0.0. On an instance upgraded from 14.x or earlier
# every session is invalidated unless you set this back to
# `gitea_incredible`.
FORGEJO__security__COOKIE_REMEMBER_NAME=persistent

# Days a "remember me" cookie stays valid.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__security__LOGIN_REMEMBER_DAYS=31

# Hash used for new passwords. Empty selects the build's default. Values
# carry tuning parameters, e.g. `argon2$2$65536$8$50`; an unknown value is
# fatal at startup.
FORGEJO__security__PASSWORD_HASH_ALGO=

# Minimum length for locally-managed passwords.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__security__MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH=8

# Character classes a password must contain, comma-separated
# (`lower,upper,digit,spec`). The default `off` means no class requirement.
FORGEJO__security__PASSWORD_COMPLEXITY=off

# Check new passwords against HaveIBeenPwned's k-anonymity API. Makes an
# outbound request on every password set, which conflicts with
# OFFLINE_MODE's intent, and fails closed if the API is unreachable.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__security__PASSWORD_CHECK_PWN=false

# Block the repository-level "git hooks" editor. Default `true`: a git hook
# runs arbitrary code as the Forgejo user, so only turn this off if every
# user who can administer a repository is already trusted with shell access.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__security__DISABLE_GIT_HOOKS=true

# Block webhook creation entirely (webhooks can be used to probe the
# internal network from the server's vantage point).
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__security__DISABLE_WEBHOOKS=false

# Reject API tokens passed as a `?token=` query parameter, where they end up
# in access logs. Default false for compatibility; true is the safer setting.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__security__DISABLE_QUERY_AUTH_TOKEN=false

# Headers carrying the authenticated identity when
# `[service] ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION` is on. Only meaningful
# when a proxy you control strips them from client requests first;
# otherwise anyone can send the header and become anyone.
FORGEJO__security__REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_USER=X-WEBAUTH-USER
FORGEJO__security__REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_EMAIL=X-WEBAUTH-EMAIL
FORGEJO__security__REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_FULL_NAME=X-WEBAUTH-FULLNAME

# How many proxies deep to trust when reading X-Forwarded-For, and which
# CIDRs/IPs are allowed to set it. The first-boot template ships
# `REVERSE_PROXY_TRUSTED_PROXIES = *`, which trusts everything. Narrow it to
# otterdeploy's proxy once you know its address, or client IPs in the audit
# log are whatever the client claimed.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__security__REVERSE_PROXY_LIMIT=1
FORGEJO__security__REVERSE_PROXY_TRUSTED_PROXIES=*

# Require pushes to carry Forgejo's own environment (set by its hooks),
# which stops pushes made directly on the server's filesystem from being
# processed as if they came through Forgejo.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__security__ONLY_ALLOW_PUSH_IF_GITEA_ENVIRONMENT_SET=true

# ─── Users, registration & sign-in ([service]) ─────────────────────────────

# Close self-service sign-up. The usual setting for a private instance: turn
# it on after creating the accounts you need, and invite via admin instead.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("Service configuration", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/config-cheat-sheet/)
FORGEJO__service__DISABLE_REGISTRATION=false

# Require a login for every page, so nothing is public. A plain boolean in
# Forgejo. Gitea's `expensive` mode does not exist here.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW=false

# Require new users to confirm their email before the account activates.
# Needs a working [mailer] below, or nobody can ever sign in.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__REGISTER_EMAIL_CONFIRM=false

# Hold new registrations for an administrator to approve. Ignored when
# REGISTER_EMAIL_CONFIRM is on, since email confirmation wins.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__REGISTER_MANUAL_CONFIRM=false

# Send notification email for issue/PR activity. Off by default even when
# the mailer is configured.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__ENABLE_NOTIFY_MAIL=false

# Allow HTTP Basic auth (username + password or token) against the API and
# git-over-HTTP. Turning it off leaves OAuth/session auth only, which breaks
# `git clone` over HTTPS with a token.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__ENABLE_BASIC_AUTHENTICATION=true

# Trust an authenticating reverse proxy's headers as the login. Turn this on
# ONLY once REVERSE_PROXY_TRUSTED_PROXIES above is narrowed, and only if the
# proxy strips the auth headers from inbound client requests.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION=false
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_AUTO_REGISTRATION=false

# Show a CAPTCHA on the registration form, and pick which one. `image` is
# the built-in one and needs no third-party keys; the others need their own
# sitekey/secret pair (FORGEJO__service__RECAPTCHA_SITEKEY,
# FORGEJO__service__CF_TURNSTILE_SECRET, and so on) and reach out to a
# third party on every sign-up.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__ENABLE_CAPTCHA=false
# @type=enum(image, recaptcha, hcaptcha, mcaptcha, cfturnstile)
FORGEJO__service__CAPTCHA_TYPE=image

# Hide new users' email addresses by default.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__DEFAULT_KEEP_EMAIL_PRIVATE=false

# Let ordinary users create organizations.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__DEFAULT_ALLOW_CREATE_ORGANIZATION=true

# Visibility new accounts get. Empty uses the first entry of
# ALLOWED_USER_VISIBILITY_MODES, i.e. `public`.
# @type=enum(public, limited, private)
FORGEJO__service__DEFAULT_USER_VISIBILITY=

# Domain used to build the `noreply` address that hides a user's real email
# in commits. Empty derives it from [server] DOMAIN as `noreply.<domain>`.
FORGEJO__service__NO_REPLY_ADDRESS=

# Comma-separated glob lists of email domains allowed (or blocked) at
# registration. Empty means no restriction.
FORGEJO__service__EMAIL_DOMAIN_ALLOWLIST=
FORGEJO__service__EMAIL_DOMAIN_BLOCKLIST=

# Adds Forgejo's bundled list of disposable/throwaway email providers to the
# blocklist. A Forgejo addition, and the cheapest spam control on an open
# instance.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__service__EMAIL_DOMAIN_BLOCK_DISPOSABLE=false

# ─── Outgoing email ([mailer]) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is set by the compose: an instance without a mailer still
# works, it just cannot send confirmations, password resets or
# notifications.

# Master switch. Every other key in this section is ignored while it is off.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("Email setup", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/setup/email/)
FORGEJO__mailer__ENABLED=false

# Transport. Empty is inferred from SMTP_PORT (25 -> smtp, 465 -> smtps,
# 587 -> smtp+starttls, anything else -> smtps with a logged error), so set
# it explicitly. `sendmail` shells out to SENDMAIL_PATH instead of using
# SMTP; `dummy` logs the message and sends nothing, which is useful for
# testing the flow.
# @type=enum(smtp, smtps, smtp+starttls, smtp+unix, sendmail, dummy)
FORGEJO__mailer__PROTOCOL=

# SMTP host, and port. An empty port is inferred from PROTOCOL (smtp -> 25,
# smtps -> 465, smtp+starttls -> 587).
FORGEJO__mailer__SMTP_ADDR=
# @type=port
FORGEJO__mailer__SMTP_PORT=

# SMTP credentials. Most providers want the full email address as the
# username and an app-specific password. PASSWD_URI is the file-backed form
# (`file:/run/secrets/smtp`), and setting both it and PASSWD is fatal.
FORGEJO__mailer__USER=
# @sensitive
FORGEJO__mailer__PASSWD=
FORGEJO__mailer__PASSWD_URI=

# Envelope/header From. Accepts a bare address or `Name <addr>`. Empty falls
# back to USER, which is wrong for providers that require a verified sender.
FORGEJO__mailer__FROM=

# Hostname sent in the SMTP HELO/EHLO. Empty uses the container's hostname,
# which some strict relays reject. ENABLE_HELO=false skips the greeting
# entirely.
FORGEJO__mailer__HELO_HOSTNAME=
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__mailer__ENABLE_HELO=true

# Accept any server certificate, including self-signed ones. Only for an
# internal relay you control; it disables the TLS trust check.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__mailer__FORCE_TRUST_SERVER_CERT=false

# Prefix prepended to every outgoing subject line, e.g. "[Forgejo] ".
FORGEJO__mailer__SUBJECT_PREFIX=

# ─── Actions (built-in CI) ([actions]) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Forgejo Actions is enabled by default at this version, but it does nothing
# until at least one Forgejo Runner is registered against the instance.
# Unlike Gitea, there is no environment variable that pre-seeds a
# registration token. Take one from Site Administration or
# `forgejo forgejo-cli actions generate-runner-token`.

# @type=boolean
# @docs("Forgejo Actions administrator guide", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/actions/)
FORGEJO__actions__ENABLED=true

# Where a bare `uses: owner/action@ref` is resolved from. The Forgejo
# default is the project's own mirror at https://data.forgejo.org; `github`
# means github.com and `self` resolves against this instance's own ROOT_URL.
# Any other full URL is used verbatim.
# @docs("Forgejo Runner registration", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/actions/registration/)
FORGEJO__actions__DEFAULT_ACTIONS_URL=https://data.forgejo.org

# Days workflow logs and uploaded artifacts are kept before cleanup.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__actions__LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=365
# @type=number
FORGEJO__actions__ARTIFACT_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# Compression applied to stored job logs. `zstd` (the default) or `none`;
# any other value is fatal at startup.
# @type=enum(zstd, none)
FORGEJO__actions__LOG_COMPRESSION=zstd

# How long a task may go without contacting the server, run without
# finishing, or sit unclaimed before Forgejo gives up on it. Duration
# strings.
FORGEJO__actions__ZOMBIE_TASK_TIMEOUT=10m
FORGEJO__actions__ENDLESS_TASK_TIMEOUT=3h
FORGEJO__actions__ABANDONED_JOB_TIMEOUT=24h

# Commit-message markers that skip a workflow run, comma-separated.
FORGEJO__actions__SKIP_WORKFLOW_STRINGS=[skip ci],[ci skip],[no ci],[skip actions],[actions skip]

# ─── Federation ([federation]) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# ActivityPub federation between Forgejo instances. Forgejo-only, and still
# experimental at v15, so it stays off unless you deliberately turn it on.

# @type=boolean
# @docs("Configuration Cheat Sheet: federation", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/config-cheat-sheet/)
FORGEJO__federation__ENABLED=false

# Whether this instance publishes per-user activity counts to federated
# peers. Only read when ENABLED is on.
# @type=boolean
FORGEJO__federation__SHARE_USER_STATISTICS=true

# Maximum size, in MiB, of a federated payload this instance will accept.
# @type=number
FORGEJO__federation__MAX_SIZE=4

# ─── Logging ([log]) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated list of log outputs. `console` is what a container wants:
# it puts the log on stdout where `docker logs` and otterdeploy's log view
# can see it. `file` writes into the data volume instead and the container
# then looks silent.
# @docs("Logging documentation", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/troubleshooting/logging/)
FORGEJO__log__MODE=console

# @type=enum(trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal, none)
FORGEJO__log__LEVEL=info

# Level at or above which a stack trace is attached to the log line.
# `none` (the default) never attaches one.
# @type=enum(trace, debug, info, warn, error, fatal, none)
FORGEJO__log__STACKTRACE_LEVEL=none

# Directory for file-mode logs, inside the container.
FORGEJO__log__ROOT_PATH=/data/gitea/log

# ─── Container runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plain variables read by the image's entrypoint and by the Go binary, NOT
# mapped into app.ini. Values shown as defaults come from the Dockerfile.

# Numeric uid/gid the entrypoint rewrites the in-container `git` user to
# before starting Forgejo. The compose pins both to 1000 so the files on the
# data volume have a stable, non-root owner; change them only to match a
# bind-mounted /data owned by a specific host user.
# @type=number
# @docs("Installation with Docker", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/installation/docker/)
USER_UID=1000
# @type=number
USER_GID=1000

# Account name Forgejo runs as inside the container; the image sets `git`
# and the entrypoint renames the passwd entry if you change it. It also ends
# up in SSH clone URLs. Changing it on an existing volume leaves file
# ownership behind.
USER=git

# Custom/config directory. The image sets /data/gitea, which is where the
# data volume is mounted and where app.ini is written; the s6 setup script
# uses it to locate ${GITEA_CUSTOM}/conf/app.ini. Repointing it without
# moving the volume loses the configuration. FORGEJO_CUSTOM is the
# fork-branded alias, only consulted when GITEA_CUSTOM is empty, and the s6
# scripts read GITEA_CUSTOM directly, so on this image set that one.
GITEA_CUSTOM=/data/gitea
FORGEJO_CUSTOM=

# Absolute path of Forgejo's working directory. Unset in the root image (it
# derives the work path from the binary location); the rootless image sets
# /var/lib/gitea. Must be absolute. A relative value is fatal at startup.
# FORGEJO_WORK_DIR is the alias, consulted only when GITEA_WORK_DIR is empty.
GITEA_WORK_DIR=
FORGEJO_WORK_DIR=

# ROOTLESS IMAGE ONLY (Dockerfile.rootless). This template runs the root
# image, whose s6 scripts hardcode ${GITEA_CUSTOM}/conf/app.ini, so setting
# these here changes nothing. Declared so the difference between the two
# images is visible.
GITEA_APP_INI=
GITEA_TEMP=

# Overrides the app.ini `RUN_MODE`, checked before the config file. Anything
# other than `dev` is treated as production, deliberately, so a typo cannot
# accidentally expose dev behaviour. There is no FORGEJO_RUN_MODE alias.
# @type=enum(prod, dev)
GITEA_RUN_MODE=

# Escape hatch that lets Forgejo start as uid 0. It refuses to run as root
# otherwise, and that refusal is not a warning to silence. Use this only
# while debugging a broken volume permission. No FORGEJO_ alias.
# @type=boolean
GITEA_I_AM_BEING_UNSAFE_RUNNING_AS_ROOT=false

# ─── First-boot app.ini template ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by docker/root/etc/s6/gitea/setup and substituted into
# /etc/templates/app.ini, but ONLY when /data/gitea/conf/app.ini does not
# exist yet. On any restart with an existing data volume they are ignored,
# which is exactly why this compose uses the FORGEJO__ forms above instead.
# The values shown are the entrypoint's own fallbacks.

# @docs("Configuration Cheat Sheet", https://forgejo.org/docs/v15.0/admin/config-cheat-sheet/)
APP_NAME=Forgejo: Beyond coding. We forge.
# @type=enum(prod, dev)
RUN_MODE=prod
DOMAIN=localhost
SSH_DOMAIN=localhost
# @type=port
HTTP_PORT=3000
# The compose routes the public URL through FORGEJO__server__ROOT_URL, which
# is re-applied on every restart, so this first-boot-only twin stays empty.
# @type=url
ROOT_URL=
# @type=boolean
DISABLE_SSH=false
# @type=port
SSH_PORT=22
# Defaults to SSH_PORT when empty.
# @type=port
SSH_LISTEN_PORT=
# @type=boolean
LFS_START_SERVER=false

# @type=enum(postgres, mysql, sqlite3)
DB_TYPE=sqlite3
DB_HOST=localhost:3306
DB_NAME=gitea
DB_USER=root
# @sensitive
DB_PASSWD=

# Setting SECRET_KEY here makes the setup script flip INSTALL_LOCK to true
# on its own, which is how you get a first boot with no install page. Both
# only take effect on that first boot.
# @sensitive
SECRET_KEY=
# @type=boolean
INSTALL_LOCK=false

# @type=boolean
DISABLE_REGISTRATION=false
# @type=boolean
REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW=false

# ─── OpenSSH daemon (root image) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Substituted into /etc/ssh/sshd_config by docker/root/etc/s6/openssh/setup
# on EVERY boot, unlike the app.ini template above. SSH_PORT and
# SSH_LISTEN_PORT (declared just above) are shared with it: sshd binds
# SSH_LISTEN_PORT, defaulting to SSH_PORT.

# Written as sshd's MaxStartups / MaxSessions when non-empty; empty leaves
# the line out and sshd uses its own defaults.
SSH_MAX_STARTUPS=
SSH_MAX_SESSIONS=

# Path to an extra sshd config file to `Include`, for options this template
# does not expose. Mount the file in first.
SSH_INCLUDE_FILE=

# sshd LogLevel.
# @type=enum(QUIET, FATAL, ERROR, INFO, VERBOSE, DEBUG, DEBUG1, DEBUG2, DEBUG3)
SSH_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Paths to host-key certificates signed by an SSH CA, written as
# `HostCertificate` lines. Empty is normal; the setup script auto-detects
# /data/ssh/ssh_host_*_key-cert.pub (and the older ssh_host_*_cert names) if
# you mount certificates there, and generates plain host keys on first boot
# either way.
SSH_ED25519_CERT=
SSH_RSA_CERT=
SSH_ECDSA_CERT=
